.github/CODEOWNERS-tmp
# Symlink created by nft-utils nfcoreLink() during test runs
# nf-core modules are installed by the consuming pipeline, not vendored here -- with one
# exception. A subworkflow's `include` is resolved by Nextflow at PARSE time, so a subworkflow
# that composes an nf-core module cannot be tested at all unless that module is present, and the
# nf-test job does not install it. That is why the varpipe_core and varpipe_variantanalysis
# subworkflow tests print "Dependency ... not found" on every run and have never actually
# executed. minimap2/align is checked in so binman_bin_reads does not join them. The lint matrix
# filters on `modules/amd-ph-core/**`, so a vendored nf-core module is never linted as if it
# were ours.
modules/nf-core/*
!modules/nf-core/minimap2/
.venv*
